WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:31.157
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:31.427 --> 00:32.971
What the hell is this?

3
00:39.144 --> 00:42.647
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

4
00:42.730 --> 00:43.648
DAILY WAGE 4,012,000 WON

5
00:43.731 --> 00:46.442
Good job. Here. The pay for your shift.

6
00:48.528 --> 00:51.030
Work is such a fascinating thing.

7
00:52.657 --> 00:54.951
When you're working, you're filled with questions.

8
00:55.034 --> 00:57.829
"Can I do this? Can I survive this?" But after…

9
00:58.413 --> 01:02.959
Once you get that money in your hand, nothing else matters.

10
01:04.043 --> 01:05.086
Wouldn't you agree?

11
01:05.879 --> 01:07.338
Isn't that great?

12
01:11.176 --> 01:12.260
I, uh…

13
01:13.136 --> 01:14.846
We should talk about last night.

14
01:14.929 --> 01:17.974
Oh, we don't need to know the details from last night.

15
01:18.057 --> 01:21.227
My job is to connect people who need things.

16
01:21.311 --> 01:23.313
So, how does the connection work?

17
01:25.481 --> 01:26.733
Trade secret, my man.

18
01:26.816 --> 01:29.903
I almost died last night, and you can't say anything? Come on!

19
01:29.986 --> 01:32.322
This wasn't a gig. This was something else.

20
01:34.824 --> 01:37.952
Or did I imagine it? Please, tell me what I saw.

21
01:38.620 --> 01:39.495
Hm.

22
01:41.331 --> 01:43.875
If you really want an explanation,

23
01:45.084 --> 01:46.961
the world as you know it

24
01:47.795 --> 01:49.631
looks a little bit like this.

25
01:55.220 --> 01:56.387
There's a side we live on,

26
01:57.680 --> 01:59.098
and the other side.

27
02:00.600 --> 02:03.019
This side, the world we live in, is yang.

28
02:04.062 --> 02:05.730
And this one? Yin.

29
02:07.649 --> 02:11.069
Yin and yang are both here. However, they never meet.

30
02:15.323 --> 02:18.743
Which is why there must always be a boundary between them.

31
02:20.370 --> 02:22.956
And when that boundary becomes unstable,

32
02:23.039 --> 02:26.376
the energy from the other world invades ours,

33
02:26.459 --> 02:28.795
and strange things start to happen.

34
02:30.797 --> 02:33.716
When that energy from the other world invades,

35
02:35.009 --> 02:39.430
we send in a strong yang energy to suppress that yin energy.

36
02:40.181 --> 02:41.516
That's the job.

37
02:43.017 --> 02:47.563
Because there's no stronger yang energy than the struggle to make a living.

38
02:48.064 --> 02:49.524
Now, do you understand?

39
02:51.317 --> 02:53.319
So, Mr. Hyeok-jun,

40
02:53.820 --> 02:55.738
what sort of work would you prefer?

41
02:57.657 --> 03:01.202
I didn't… I mean, you're letting me choose?

42
03:01.286 --> 03:02.996
You want a job, don't you?

43
03:03.079 --> 03:05.748
Let me see what's available and we'll go from there.

44
03:05.832 --> 03:09.919
So maybe… Is there anything I could do during the daytime?

45
03:10.003 --> 03:11.754
Daytime. Let's see…

46
03:11.838 --> 03:13.548
Something that feels safer?

47
03:13.631 --> 03:16.634
Somewhere out in the open, so, uh, my head is clear.

48
03:16.718 --> 03:18.845
Somewhere out in the open…

49
03:25.143 --> 03:28.021
KD PHARMACEUTICAL, EVENT MANAGER 100 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 4 P.M. - 10 P.M.

50
03:28.104 --> 03:30.023
One hundred times?

51
03:30.106 --> 03:33.568
Ah, I should have mentioned this to you right away.

52
03:34.068 --> 03:35.778
Each time you complete a temp job,

53
03:35.862 --> 03:38.740
your paycheck for the next will be doubled. At least.

54
03:41.826 --> 03:42.744
Mm…

55
03:44.495 --> 03:48.082
Um… "Manager." What does that entail, exactly?

56
03:49.917 --> 03:51.753
You'll just be driving clients.

57
03:53.129 --> 03:55.089
So, you're telling me I would only be driving?

58
03:55.173 --> 03:56.883
Exactly.

59
03:56.966 --> 03:59.969
The person you'll be with is an event planner.

60
04:01.012 --> 04:04.849
You will only have to drive them to the meeting place without any problems.

61
04:09.812 --> 04:11.439
Now, what do you say?

62
04:12.148 --> 04:14.525
You need to make money, don't ya?

63
04:26.412 --> 04:28.122
ACCEPT

64
04:33.878 --> 04:35.421
Ah, sh…

65
04:42.804 --> 04:44.013
Where have you been?

66
04:46.891 --> 04:48.518
Fortune-telling and tarot?

67
04:50.436 --> 04:51.312
Huh?

68
04:52.021 --> 04:54.232
Maybe that move was too soon.

69
04:54.732 --> 04:57.527
I'm investigating the staffing agency in this building.

70
04:57.610 --> 04:59.028
Are you free?

71
05:00.863 --> 05:02.573
Mm, I would love to talk.

72
05:02.657 --> 05:05.743
Seeing your face this close, it's very dry and cracked too.

73
05:05.827 --> 05:07.578
So pale and maybe a bit dull.

74
05:08.079 --> 05:10.373
Were you pulling the horrible late-night shifts?

75
05:10.456 --> 05:13.084
Oh, no, no, no. Why are you at this building? Are you following me?

76
05:15.086 --> 05:16.462
Let's have a cup of tea.

77
05:16.546 --> 05:19.090
Ten minutes? No. Just give me five minutes of your time.

78
05:19.173 --> 05:21.384
Oh, and just one more thing.

79
05:21.467 --> 05:25.012
I have a few questions about the Spider Staffing Agency.

80
05:25.096 --> 05:27.598
If you disclose what happens on the job to any third party…

81
05:27.682 --> 05:29.142
Eum Yeon-joo is my name.

82
05:30.476 --> 05:33.104
…you will incur a penalty. Understand?

83
05:35.022 --> 05:36.274
- Here-- - Oh, oh!

84
05:36.774 --> 05:38.067
No. Thanks, but no.

85
05:45.408 --> 05:46.242
Hm.

86
06:42.173 --> 06:45.676
DEAD-END JOB

87
06:47.053 --> 06:49.972
A JOURNEY WITH A PIERROT

88
06:57.188 --> 06:58.731
Mom, I'm here!

89
06:58.814 --> 07:02.652
- Wow. And what is this, huh? - It's Hanwoo beef.

90
07:03.152 --> 07:03.986
Oh, really?

91
07:04.070 --> 07:05.696
Yeah.

92
07:08.741 --> 07:09.909
A million won.

93
07:10.493 --> 07:11.786
A million won?

94
07:12.912 --> 07:15.540
- But how? Did you get a job? - No, just temping.

95
07:15.623 --> 07:17.959
Temping, huh. Oh.

96
07:18.834 --> 07:21.754
I know, but I'll get a real job soon. It just isn't easy.

97
07:21.837 --> 07:23.464
I hope it's really soon.

98
07:24.340 --> 07:27.760
Find something you would want to do and make it into a career.

99
07:27.843 --> 07:28.928
That's the best way.

100
07:30.221 --> 07:31.806
Look at your father.

101
07:31.889 --> 07:33.641
He dabbled in everything,

102
07:33.724 --> 07:35.810
but in the end, he didn't achieve anything.

103
07:35.893 --> 07:38.521
And after all that, he still left us.

104
07:40.523 --> 07:42.316
Whoa. Uh… Uh…

105
07:43.025 --> 07:43.943
Uh… Ooh!

106
07:47.947 --> 07:48.948
Okay, then.

107
07:52.577 --> 07:53.953
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

108
07:54.036 --> 07:55.162
Oof.

109
07:57.373 --> 08:01.460
Son, how does it make you feel, watching your dad practice?

110
08:01.544 --> 08:03.462
Uh… Very excited.

111
08:03.546 --> 08:04.880
A FATHER'S MIRACLE

112
08:04.964 --> 08:07.758
So, when you grow up, will you be just like your dad?

113
08:07.842 --> 08:10.094
Yeah! I'll be just like my dad.

114
08:10.177 --> 08:11.095
Uh-huh.

115
08:11.721 --> 08:14.890
Oh, your life should be different from mine.

116
08:14.974 --> 08:16.058
Different?

117
08:16.559 --> 08:20.354
For Hyeok-jun, he'll be the opposite of me, I know.

118
08:20.855 --> 08:22.732
He'll make lots of money for his family.

119
08:23.232 --> 08:25.234
That's what it's all really about.

120
08:27.778 --> 08:29.363
Mama!

121
08:32.491 --> 08:34.952
No, your sister. What ya doing?

122
08:35.453 --> 08:39.040
Ah, shit! Will you get out? My door wasn't open.

123
08:40.833 --> 08:41.834
Why are you here?

124
08:41.917 --> 08:44.086
Oh, did you get hurt? Who did this?

125
08:44.170 --> 08:47.214
- What happened? - Stop! Mind your own business.

126
08:47.298 --> 08:48.299
Shit!

127
08:48.799 --> 08:51.177
Ugh. Again with that movie?

128
08:51.260 --> 08:52.386
Does baby miss daddy?

129
08:52.470 --> 08:55.181
Of course not. The movie must have played on its own.

130
08:55.264 --> 08:58.142
What's so great about a dad who left his family?

131
08:58.851 --> 09:00.728
This milk is basically trash. You should toss it.

132
09:00.811 --> 09:03.481
Hey, don't put that… Seriously?

133
09:03.564 --> 09:05.191
Please just tell me what you're doing here.

134
09:07.902 --> 09:09.195
I need help.

135
09:10.112 --> 09:11.906
Money? Money for pissing me off?

136
09:11.989 --> 09:14.033
For a job interview tomorrow.

137
09:14.533 --> 09:16.952
Did you expect me to go like this? Come on!

138
09:17.036 --> 09:19.372
I should at least get one thing to wear.

139
09:19.455 --> 09:23.292
You look fine. And you should never wear new clothes to an interview, because…

140
09:23.376 --> 09:24.919
because it's bad luck.

141
09:26.712 --> 09:29.131
I know you still have the money mom lent you.

142
09:29.215 --> 09:31.092
She gave it to you for a lease.

143
09:32.927 --> 09:34.095
Why would I give you the money

144
09:34.178 --> 09:36.555
when she wanted me to get a place for myself?

145
09:36.639 --> 09:40.101
Mom trusted you. She worked her head, shoulders, knees, and toes to the bone

146
09:40.184 --> 09:42.186
to pay for that down payment, and now here you are--

147
09:42.269 --> 09:45.439
Hey, are you implying I blew the money she gave me? What the hell?

148
09:48.150 --> 09:50.778
Put some bills nicely in this hand and Mom never has to know a thing.

149
09:51.862 --> 09:53.739
But… But… But… Come on.

150
09:53.823 --> 09:56.659
You invested it in stocks, didn't you, moron?

151
09:59.036 --> 10:00.162
You knew?

152
10:00.246 --> 10:01.747
Of course I knew.

153
10:02.707 --> 10:04.166
How much did you lose?

154
10:04.875 --> 10:06.752
What? Too embarrassed to admit it?

155
10:07.253 --> 10:08.504
Was it half?

156
10:09.880 --> 10:11.382
Seventy percent?

157
10:16.137 --> 10:17.054
All?

158
10:17.596 --> 10:18.723
Seriously?

159
10:18.806 --> 10:20.975
I'm in the middle of making it back, okay?

160
10:21.058 --> 10:23.018
You're out of your mind.

161
10:23.102 --> 10:24.103
Stay here tonight.

162
10:24.186 --> 10:25.229
Make your job interview,

163
10:25.312 --> 10:27.565
and then I'll give you the money when I get back.

164
10:27.648 --> 10:30.276
- Where are you going? - I have plans.

165
10:30.359 --> 10:32.194
What? Are you going to a temp job?

166
10:32.278 --> 10:34.613
- I have plans. - You're not doing anything crazy?

167
10:34.697 --> 10:35.698
And don't get into fights!

168
10:35.781 --> 10:37.158
- It's not like that! - Damn.

169
10:38.659 --> 10:40.286
What does he mean it's not like that?

170
10:40.369 --> 10:42.621
I can tell something happened just by looking at him.

171
11:01.766 --> 11:03.684
KD Pharmaceutical?

172
11:04.769 --> 11:06.270
Is this the right place?

173
11:06.353 --> 11:09.440
KD PHARMACEUTICAL EVENT MANAGER 100 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE

174
11:09.523 --> 11:11.984
STARTS AT 4 P.M. ENDS AT 10 P.M.

175
11:20.159 --> 11:22.536
I go from a rat to a pig now?

176
11:34.882 --> 11:36.300
Uh, hello.

177
11:36.383 --> 11:38.511
On time is already late.

178
11:38.594 --> 11:40.888
Oh, I can't believe this.

179
11:42.765 --> 11:44.600
- Who do you think you are? - Sorry?

180
11:45.100 --> 11:48.354
I said… who do you think you are?

181
11:50.898 --> 11:51.941
Oh, of course.

182
11:52.024 --> 11:55.277
My name is Byeon Hyeok-jun. I'm 30. Years old, I mean.

183
11:55.361 --> 11:57.363
Do you think I asked for your introduction?

184
11:58.155 --> 12:00.825
A salaried employee can't clock out, stuck waiting for the temp,

185
12:00.908 --> 12:02.243
and you have the nerve to be late?

186
12:02.326 --> 12:04.870
Oh, so sorry, but I just got the call a few minutes ago, so--

187
12:04.954 --> 12:08.290
Your company didn't make it clear that Mr. Jo has a bad fucking temper?

188
12:09.625 --> 12:11.043
Uh, no, but I…

189
12:12.044 --> 12:12.962
Shit.

190
12:13.754 --> 12:14.839
Mm.

191
12:16.632 --> 12:17.633
Huh?

192
12:18.759 --> 12:19.885
Come on.

193
12:20.511 --> 12:21.971
Hurry up now.

194
12:24.056 --> 12:27.101
Since you seem to operate outside society, I'll teach you.

195
12:27.184 --> 12:30.145
Did a dumbass like you even go to school?

196
12:30.229 --> 12:31.397
A local community college.

197
12:31.480 --> 12:35.150
Well, I went to a four-year university in Seoul and got this important position.

198
12:35.985 --> 12:39.947
And this event we're going to? University hospital department's retreat.

199
12:40.030 --> 12:42.324
And these gifted bastards are the best in Korea.

200
12:42.825 --> 12:43.993
See my point?

201
12:46.787 --> 12:48.497
Oh, they're talented.

202
12:50.457 --> 12:51.542
Like me.

203
12:52.418 --> 12:53.502
That's what you mean, right?

204
12:55.129 --> 12:56.213
Yeah, like you?

205
12:56.797 --> 12:58.841
Come on! In the Republic of Korea,

206
12:58.924 --> 13:01.719
your intelligence determines where you'll be in life.

207
13:01.802 --> 13:04.889
They're at the top, I'm in the middle, and you're at the bottom.

208
13:05.389 --> 13:07.182
Understand? The bottom!

209
13:07.266 --> 13:09.727
Oh. Yeah, I'm last.

210
13:12.187 --> 13:14.064
Go to the snack bar and get me coffee, idiot.

211
13:14.565 --> 13:17.151
Damn. No wonder he's still a temp.

212
13:34.376 --> 13:36.170
I can't believe this.

213
13:36.670 --> 13:37.630
I'm starving.

214
13:37.713 --> 13:39.965
Better get here now or else I'll make 'em pay.

215
13:40.466 --> 13:41.675
Ah, God!

216
13:41.759 --> 13:44.219
What the hell? Come on!

217
14:02.196 --> 14:03.572
What are you?

218
14:03.656 --> 14:05.407
"Jolly Pierrot."

219
14:05.491 --> 14:07.493
"Expert mime."

220
14:09.036 --> 14:10.037
Huh.

221
14:10.829 --> 14:13.123
Jolly? This fucking crazy bastard.

222
14:14.166 --> 14:15.167
Hey, mime?

223
14:15.668 --> 14:17.586
You can speak, right? Huh?

224
14:17.670 --> 14:20.297
Since you're late, you should damn well apologize first.

225
14:21.507 --> 14:23.550
Oh. Huh?

226
14:26.887 --> 14:28.931
What's the matter with this crazy idiot?

227
14:29.014 --> 14:31.058
Hey, what is he doing? Huh?

228
14:31.141 --> 14:33.727
Your boss must be crazy. Who has seniority here?

229
14:33.811 --> 14:35.688
Ah, shit. I don't have time for this.

230
14:35.771 --> 14:37.606
We've got to go or we'll be late.

231
14:37.690 --> 14:40.859
You two, if you fuck this up for me, I'll rip you both to shreds!

232
14:40.943 --> 14:42.319
Got it? Huh?

233
14:42.903 --> 14:46.699
Hurry up. We're already late. Damn it! You trying to get me fired?

234
15:03.132 --> 15:05.384
So, you're saying I would only be driving?

235
15:07.386 --> 15:08.679
Yes, that's right.

236
15:09.179 --> 15:12.307
And in order to get paid, you must stay until the end.

237
15:14.601 --> 15:18.689
Leave the rest to the event planner and they will take care of everything.

238
15:25.362 --> 15:29.158
PANG PANG EVENTS

239
15:39.001 --> 15:39.960
Stop!

240
15:41.128 --> 15:44.840
I'm fucking trapped with not one, but two clowns in this car. Damn.

241
15:44.923 --> 15:47.968
You will behave, or else…

242
15:48.969 --> 15:51.096
SHINIL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL PROF. YOON

243
15:52.389 --> 15:55.017
Hello! Yes, Professor. Yes, yes, sir.

244
15:55.100 --> 15:57.019
Yes, sir. I'm on my way.

245
15:57.770 --> 16:01.231
My apologies. I'm flying down the highway as we speak.

246
16:01.315 --> 16:04.693
I kid you not, they will go bananas over the MC we hired.

247
16:04.777 --> 16:06.487
He'll really get the crowd going.

248
16:06.987 --> 16:10.199
Oh, you know I can't miss out on this. Yes! Let's go all night, sir!

249
16:11.784 --> 16:12.910
You're the best!

250
16:12.993 --> 16:13.952
Love you!

251
16:14.036 --> 16:15.871
Yes.

252
16:20.959 --> 16:23.587
It's just every damn time with this, shitheads!

253
16:23.670 --> 16:25.506
Fuck me! "Where are you?"

254
16:25.589 --> 16:27.883
I said I'm on my way! Ugh!

255
16:27.966 --> 16:30.052
Fucking bastards, all of these guys.

256
16:41.939 --> 16:43.440
Did you just laugh?

257
16:45.275 --> 16:47.319
I'm having to act like some professor's servant

258
16:47.820 --> 16:49.279
and you're laughing?

259
16:49.363 --> 16:50.864
You both are getting fired.

260
16:50.948 --> 16:53.492
I will call your boss and make him fire you two.

261
16:53.575 --> 16:54.618
Who's laughing now?

262
16:55.869 --> 16:56.745
Okay.

263
16:57.329 --> 16:59.206
What the? Where is it?

264
17:04.336 --> 17:07.464
What the hell? Give it back. Give me my phone!

265
17:07.548 --> 17:09.383
What are you trying… Stop!

266
17:09.466 --> 17:11.677
Give it… I'm calling your damn boss!

267
17:12.302 --> 17:15.180
This guy's a lunatic. Hey, temp, stop the car.

268
17:15.264 --> 17:16.932
Pull over right now. Oh, piss off!

269
17:17.015 --> 17:19.560
- Give me the phone! Come on! - Whoa!

270
17:20.686 --> 17:21.979
If you don't give it--

271
17:23.105 --> 17:24.523
Oh, shit!

272
17:25.023 --> 17:26.733
Damn, you idiot!

273
17:29.403 --> 17:30.821
What's wrong with this?

274
17:34.283 --> 17:36.201
It won't stop! What's going on?

275
17:42.666 --> 17:44.751
Why is this happening?

276
17:44.835 --> 17:46.420
What are you doing?!

277
17:46.503 --> 17:49.006
Agh! I can't control it. The car's moving on its own!

278
17:49.089 --> 17:50.299
It's not me!

279
17:50.382 --> 17:52.384
I don't care. Just make it stop the car!

280
17:52.467 --> 17:55.012
Whoo!

281
17:55.095 --> 17:56.388
Crazy bastards!

282
18:02.686 --> 18:04.980
Oh God, just pull over!

283
18:06.690 --> 18:08.108
- Oh! - What the…

284
18:08.192 --> 18:09.484
Bunny! That bunny!

285
18:10.360 --> 18:12.237
From the street! That's the--

286
18:41.308 --> 18:43.018
Oh God. Rest stop.

287
18:44.102 --> 18:45.270
Whoa!

288
18:45.354 --> 18:47.314
REST STOP

289
18:50.734 --> 18:52.319
Damn it! Get out.

290
18:53.528 --> 18:55.322
Hey, hey, give me my phone.

291
18:55.822 --> 18:57.282
I said get out now!

292
18:58.700 --> 18:59.660
Ah.

293
19:01.745 --> 19:04.289
Hey, you, what are you…

294
19:06.750 --> 19:08.126
Oh, now you want to grovel?

295
19:08.210 --> 19:12.089
Remember who's in charge here, huh? I should just stop this right now.

296
19:12.589 --> 19:15.133
You think those cheap tricks are funny, huh?

297
19:15.217 --> 19:16.093
Huh?

298
19:17.052 --> 19:19.554
My phone. Give me my phone.

299
19:20.889 --> 19:21.723
Oh.

300
19:22.516 --> 19:23.350
Oh!

301
19:24.393 --> 19:25.269
Oh.

302
